-- An HTTP/1.1 server, written over std.net's sockets: a listener's
-- connections accepted one at a time, each one's requests read in turn
-- -- the request line, the headers, and a body of the length its
-- `Content-Length` says, or sent in chunks -- each given to a handler, and its response
-- written with its length, the connection kept for the next request
-- unless it is to be closed (HTTP/1.0, or `Connection: close`), and
-- closed by the `with` holding it when it is done.  So it is the C
-- backend's alone, as std.net is.  Import it by a name, `import
-- std.http.server as Server`, beside `import std.http as HTTP`, whose
-- `Response` a handler gives, whole, in a `Reply`.  A server of many connections at once is
-- a module of its own: std.http.bocserver's reads each a piece at a
-- time, by `requestIn`, every wait an act boc's behaviours await.
--
-- ```haskell
-- import co
-- import custodian as Custodian
-- import exception
-- import std.http as HTTP
-- import std.http.server as Server
-- import std.net as Net
-- import std.time as Time
--
-- hello : {e : HFunctor} -> Server.Request -> Co e (Server.Reply e)
-- hello r = pure (Whole (Server.plain 200 ("hello, " ^ r.target ^ "\n")))
--
-- -- | `hello` served on the port, until a connection cannot be accepted,
-- -- | or the port not listened on: then that is thrown
-- helloAt : {e : HFunctor}
--         -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
--         -> {{clock : Time.time <: e}}
--         -> {{fail : exception Net.NetError <: e}}
--         -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: e}}
--         -> Int
--         -> Co e Unit
-- helloAt port = do
--   r <- Net.withListener { host = "127.0.0.1", port = port } 64 (\l -> Server.serve l hello)
--   either throw pure r
-- ```
--
-- A handler answers with a `Reply`, which is one of three: a response
-- whole (`Whole`); a head -- a status and headers, a `Head` -- and a body
-- given a piece at a time (`Streamed`); or a head, after which the
-- connection is the handler's (`TakenOver`).
--
-- A streamed body is a computation that yields each piece, stream's
-- `yield` of `Bytes`, and the server writes each piece as it is
-- yielded: a chunk of `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` to an HTTP/1.1
-- request, the connection kept for the next request after the last
-- chunk; to an HTTP/1.0 request, no length, the connection closed after
-- the last piece.  To a `HEAD`, and for a status with no body (204,
-- 304), the head is written alone and the body not run.  Should a piece
-- not be written -- the client gone, or not reading within `idle` -- the
-- write's `NetError` is thrown in the body, at its `yield`: a `try` there
-- hears it, and its `with`s let go of what they hold, as a throw leaves
-- them.  The server hears what the body throws of `NetError` itself, and
-- closes the connection; what it throws of another type is not the
-- server's.  So `serveConnection` asks for `exception Net.NetError`, as
-- `serve` and `serveUntil` do.
--
-- ```haskell
-- import bytes as Bytes
-- import co
-- import std.http.server as Server
-- import stream as Stream
--
-- -- | lines `i` to `n`, a piece each
-- counted : {e : HFunctor} -> {{ys : Stream.yielding Bytes <: e}} -> Int -> Int -> Co e Unit
-- counted i n =
--   if i > n then pure MkUnit
--   else do
--     Stream.yield (Bytes.fromString ("line " ^ debug i ^ "\n"))
--     counted (i + 1) n
--
-- numbered : {e : HFunctor} -> Server.Request -> Co e (Server.Reply e)
-- numbered r =
--   pure
--     (Streamed
--        { status = 200, headers = [MkPair "Content-Type" "text/plain"] }
--        (counted 1 100))
-- ```
--
-- A connection taken over is written the head the handler gave -- its
-- status and its headers as they are, no length, no `Connection` of the
-- server's: `101 Switching Protocols`, `Connection: Upgrade`, say --
-- and then given to the handler's function, a `Taken`: the request, the
-- connection, and what was read of it after the request.  The server
-- reads no more of it, nor writes; once the function is done, the
-- connection is closed by the `with` holding it.  How long the other
-- side may be silent is then the function's to say.
--
-- A request's body is read whole before the handler is given it: as
-- long as its `Content-Length` says, or, sent in chunks
-- (`Transfer-Encoding: chunked`), until its last chunk, each chunk's
-- extensions and the trailer after the last let go of -- a trailer's
-- fields are not the request's headers -- its `body` the chunks' data.
-- Where the client waits for `100 Continue` before it sends the body,
-- the server writes it once the head is read.  A request is refused,
-- and its connection closed: in chunks and with a `Content-Length` too,
-- or in chunks to HTTP/1.0, `400`, as either may be what another reader
-- of the request, a proxy before the server, went by; in another coding
-- (`gzip`), `501 Not Implemented`; a chunk not as RFC 9112 says it, or
-- its size's line longer than 4 KiB, `400`; a head longer than 64 KiB,
-- `431`; a body longer than 64 MiB, `413`, its chunks' data counted; a
-- request that is no HTTP/1.x, `400` or `505`.  Before it is closed,
-- the server shuts its side down and reads what the client still sends
-- -- a mebibyte of it at most -- so that the client is not reset before
-- it has read the response.
--
-- A connection whose client sends nothing for `idle` milliseconds -- 30
-- seconds unless a server is given another, by name, `Server.serve (idle
-- := 5000) l handle`; 0 for no limit -- is closed: between requests,
-- within a request's head or its body, and while what it still sends is
-- read before its connection is closed.  A response is written within the
-- same limit, each piece of a streamed body within it too; while a
-- response is written, the client is not read, and its silence closes
-- nothing.  So a client that holds a connection and is silent holds
-- it no longer than that, by a scheduler that waits on the world through
-- std.reactor or by none.  A client that is not silent, but sends a
-- request's head a little at a time, is held to a limit of its own: the
-- whole head is read within `headerWithin` milliseconds -- 30 seconds
-- unless another is given, by name; 0 for no limit -- of the
-- connection's start, or of the response before it, or the connection
-- is closed, unanswered, as one silent too long is.  So a server's
-- world has std.time's clock, `time`, beside std.net's `net`.

module std.http.server
  ( Request
  , header
  , plain
  , parseHead
  , BodyIs(..)
  , HeadRead(..)
  , Got(..)
  , Wanted(..)
  , requestIn
  , Chunks
  , chunks
  , Dechunked(..)
  , feedChunks
  , reason
  , responseBytes
  , chunk
  , Head
  , streamedHead
  , takeoverHead
  , keptAlive
  , After(..)
  , Taken
  , Reply(..)
  , serveConnection
  , serveUntil
  , serve
  )
import bytes as Bytes
import co
import custodian as Custodian
import exception
import std.duration as Duration
import std.http as HTTP
import std.net as Net
import std.time as Time
import stream as Stream
import uint8 as UInt8
import resource

-- | A request, as a server is sent it: its method (`GET`), its target as
-- | the request line says it (`/items?id=3`), its version (`HTTP/1.1`),
-- | its headers (a name and a value each, in their order), its body,
-- | and where it came from.  (std.http's `Request` is a client's: a URL,
-- | a time to wait, redirects followed.)
type Request =
  { method : String
  , target : String
  , version : String
  , headers : List (Pair String String)
  , body : Bytes
  , peer : Net.Address
  }

-- | The first header of that name, its case not minded (an ASCII
-- | name's), if there is one.
header : String -> Request -> Maybe String
header name r = HTTP.headerIn name r.headers

-- | A response of text, `text/plain`, UTF-8.
-- | >>> (plain 404 "no such item").headers
-- | [MkPair "Content-Type" "text/plain; charset=utf-8"]
plain : Int -> String -> HTTP.Response
plain status t =
  { status = status
  , headers = [MkPair "Content-Type" "text/plain; charset=utf-8"]
  , body = Bytes.fromString t
  }

-- Limits
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (a head's most, its lines and the blank one after them)
headMost : Int
headMost = 65536

-- (a body's most)
bodyMost : Int
bodyMost = 67108864

-- (how much is read at a time)
readSize : Int
readSize = 65536

-- (how much is read at a time of a head not read all at once: so a
-- client sending its head a little at a time is waited for with a small
-- buffer, not `readSize`)
headPiece : Int
headPiece = 4096

-- (how much of what a client still sends, after a request refused, is
-- read and let go of before its connection is closed)
drainMost : Int
drainMost = 1048576

-- Reading a request
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (whether the byte at `i` is `c`)
byteIs : Bytes -> Int -> Int -> Bool
byteIs b i c = UInt8.toInt (Bytes.bytesAt b i) == c

-- (where the blank line after the head starts, `\r\n\r\n`, from `i` on;
-- -1 where it is not yet)
headEnd : Bytes -> Int -> Int
headEnd b i =
  if i + 4 > Bytes.length b then 0 - 1
  else if byteIs b i 13
          && byteIs b (i + 1) 10
          && byteIs b (i + 2) 13
          && byteIs b (i + 3) 10
  then i
  else headEnd b (i + 1)

-- (a header line, `Name: value`: its name, with no space in it, and its
-- value, trimmed)
headerLine : String -> Maybe (Pair String String)
headerLine l = headerAt (indexOf ":" l 0)
  where
  -- (a header line's name, up to `i`, and its value after it)
  headerAt : Maybe Int -> Maybe (Pair String String)
  headerAt Nothing = Nothing
  headerAt (Just i) =
    let name = strSlice l 0 i
    in if i == 0 || contains " " name || contains "\t" name then Nothing
    else Just (MkPair name (trim (strSlice l (i + 1) (strLength l))))

consBoth : {a : Type} -> Maybe a -> Maybe (List a) -> Maybe (List a)
consBoth (Just x) (Just xs) = Just (x :: xs)
consBoth _ _ = Nothing

-- (each line a header's, or none)
headerLines : List String -> Maybe (List (Pair String String))
headerLines [] = Just Nil
headerLines (l :: rest) = consBoth (headerLine l) (headerLines rest)

-- (a request of its line's three parts and its headers, its body to come)
requestOf : Net.Address
          -> List String
          -> Maybe (List (Pair String String))
          -> Maybe Request
requestOf peer [m, t, v] (Just hs) =
  if strLength m == 0 || strLength t == 0 then Nothing
  else Just
      { method = m
      , target = t
      , version = v
      , headers = hs
      , body = Bytes.empty
      , peer = peer
      }
requestOf peer _ _ = Nothing

headOfLines : Net.Address -> List String -> Maybe Request
headOfLines peer [] = Nothing
headOfLines peer (l :: rest) = requestOf peer (split " " l) (headerLines rest)

-- | A request's head, its lines without the blank one after them: its
-- | method, target, version and headers, its body to come; none where
-- | it is no request's.
-- | >>> maybe "none" (\(r : Request) -> r.method ^ " " ^ r.target) (parseHead { host = "::1", port = 1 } "GET /a?b HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: x\r\nX-Y:  z ")
-- | "GET /a?b"
-- | >>> maybe Nil (\(r : Request) -> r.headers) (parseHead { host = "::1", port = 1 } "GET / HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: x\r\nX-Y:  z ")
-- | [MkPair "Host" "x", MkPair "X-Y" "z"]
-- | >>> maybe "none" (\(r : Request) -> r.method) (parseHead { host = "::1", port = 1 } "GET  HTTP/1.1")
-- | "none"
parseHead : Net.Address -> String -> Maybe Request
parseHead peer text = headOfLines peer (split "\r\n" text)

-- (what a request's head says of its body: its length, that it is sent
-- in chunks, or the status it is answered with, its connection then
-- closed)
data BodyIs = Length Int | Chunked | Refuse Int

sized : Maybe Int -> BodyIs
sized Nothing = Refuse 400
sized (Just n) =
  if n < 0 then Refuse 400 else if n > bodyMost then Refuse 413 else Length n

lengthOf : Maybe String -> BodyIs
lengthOf Nothing = Length 0
lengthOf (Just s) = sized (parseInt s)

isSome : {a : Type} -> Maybe a -> Bool
isSome m = maybe False (\_ -> True) m

-- (the codings a `Transfer-Encoding` header names, where it is one)
codingsIn : Pair String String -> List String
codingsIn (MkPair n v) =
  if HTTP.sameName n "Transfer-Encoding" then split "," v else Nil

-- (the codings a request's `Transfer-Encoding` headers name, all of
-- them, in their order, none empty)
codings : List (Pair String String) -> List String
codings hs =
  List.keepIf
    (\t -> strLength t > 0)
    (List.map trim (List.concatMap codingsIn hs))

isChunked : String -> Bool
isChunked t = HTTP.sameName t "chunked"

-- (a body in the codings named: in chunks, where `chunked` is the one;
-- `501` where another is named, which is not known; else `400`, as
-- `chunked` twice, or none)
codingsOf : List String -> BodyIs
codingsOf [t] = if isChunked t then Chunked else Refuse 501
codingsOf ts = if List.all isChunked ts then Refuse 400 else Refuse 501

-- (a body in chunks, where nothing else of the request says how long it
-- is: a `Content-Length` beside the chunks, which another reader of the
-- request may have gone by, or HTTP/1.0, which has no chunks, is `400`)
chunkedOnly : Request -> BodyIs -> BodyIs
chunkedOnly r Chunked =
  if strEq r.version "HTTP/1.0" || isSome (header "content-length" r)
  then Refuse 400
  else Chunked
chunkedOnly r is = is

bodyOf : Request -> BodyIs
bodyOf r =
  if not (strEq r.version "HTTP/1.1" || strEq r.version "HTTP/1.0")
  then Refuse (if startsWith "HTTP/" r.version then 505 else 400)
  else if isSome (header "transfer-encoding" r)
  then chunkedOnly r (codingsOf (codings r.headers))
  else lengthOf (header "content-length" r)

-- (whether the client waits for `100 Continue` before it sends its body)
expects : Request -> Bool
expects r =
  strEq r.version "HTTP/1.1"
  && maybe False (\v -> HTTP.sameName v "100-continue") (header "expect" r)

-- Reading a body sent in chunks
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (a line's most, of a chunk's size and its extensions, or of the end
-- after a chunk's data)
chunkLineMost : Int
chunkLineMost = 4096

-- (where a body sent in chunks is read to: a chunk's size line, its
-- data, so many bytes of it still to come, the line's end after the
-- data, or the trailer after the last chunk)
data ChunkAt = SizeLine | InChunk Int | ChunkEnd | InTrailer

-- | A body sent in chunks (`Transfer-Encoding: chunked`), read so far:
-- | where it is read to; a line begun, not yet ended; the data of its
-- | chunks, the last first; the data taken of the piece being read,
-- | the last first; how many bytes of data in all; and how many bytes of
-- | its trailer.
type Chunks =
  { at : ChunkAt
  , line : Bytes
  , parts : List Bytes
  , taken : List Bytes
  , size : Int
  , trailer : Int
  }

-- | A body sent in chunks, nothing of it read yet.
chunks : Chunks
chunks =
  { at = SizeLine
  , line = Bytes.empty
  , parts = Nil
  , taken = Nil
  , size = 0
  , trailer = 0
  }

-- | What a body sent in chunks comes to, a piece of it read: all read,
-- | its data, and what was read after it (`BodyRead`); more to come
-- | (`ChunksToCome`); or the status the request is answered with, its
-- | connection then closed (`ChunksRefused`).
data Dechunked = BodyRead Bytes Bytes | ChunksToCome Chunks | ChunksRefused Int

-- (a step of a piece's reading: on, from `k`; the trailer's end read,
-- the piece's rest from `k` the next request's; or done)
data ChunkStep = StepOn Chunks Int | TrailerRead Chunks Int | Stepped Dechunked

-- (where the next line feed is in `b`, from `k` on; -1 where there is
-- none)
lineFeedIn : Bytes -> Int -> Int
lineFeedIn b k =
  if k >= Bytes.length b then 0 - 1
  else if byteIs b k 10 then k
  else lineFeedIn b (k + 1)

-- (a hexadecimal digit's value, of the byte `c`; -1 where it is none)
hexValue : Int -> Int
hexValue c =
  if c >= 48 && c <= 57 then c - 48
  else if c >= 97 && c <= 102 then c - 87
  else if c >= 65 && c <= 70 then c - 55
  else 0 - 1

-- (the byte at `k` of `l` a hexadecimal digit's value; -1 where it is
-- none, or `l` ends before `k`)
hexAt : Bytes -> Int -> Int
hexAt l k =
  if k < Bytes.length l then hexValue (UInt8.toInt (Bytes.bytesAt l k))
  else 0 - 1

-- (whether `l`, from `k` on, after spaces or tabs, is an extension: `;`)
extensionAfter : Bytes -> Int -> Bool
extensionAfter l k =
  if k >= Bytes.length l then False
  else if byteIs l k 59 then True
  else if byteIs l k 32 || byteIs l k 9 then extensionAfter l (k + 1)
  else False

-- (whether `l`, from `k` on, after a chunk's size, is nothing, or its
-- extensions: `;`, after spaces or tabs, if any.  What they say is not
-- minded)
extensions : Bytes -> Int -> Bool
extensions l k = k >= Bytes.length l || extensionAfter l k

-- (a chunk's size, its hexadecimal digits in `l` from `k` on, `digits`
-- of them read, `n` so far: none where there is no digit, or what
-- follows them is not its extensions.  Past `bodyMost`, `bodyMost + 1`)
chunkSize : Bytes -> Int -> Int -> Int -> Maybe Int
chunkSize l k digits n =
  let d = hexAt l k
  in if d >= 0
  then chunkSize
      l
      (k + 1)
      (digits + 1)
      (if n * 16 + d > bodyMost then bodyMost + 1 else n * 16 + d)
  else if digits > 0 && extensions l k then Just n
  else Nothing

-- (a chunk's size read: the chunk's data next, or, at 0, the trailer;
-- past what a body may be in all, `413`)
sizeRead : Chunks -> Maybe Int -> Int -> ChunkStep
sizeRead st Nothing k = Stepped (ChunksRefused 400)
sizeRead st (Just 0) k = StepOn { st | at = InTrailer } k
sizeRead st (Just n) k =
  if st.size + n > bodyMost then Stepped (ChunksRefused 413)
  else StepOn { st | at = InChunk n, size = st.size + n } k

-- (a line read, `l`, its CRLF not in it, and the piece read on from `k`:
-- a chunk's size; the end after a chunk's data, which is empty; or a
-- line of the trailer, let go of, or its end)
lineRead : ChunkAt -> Chunks -> Bytes -> Int -> ChunkStep
lineRead SizeLine st l k = sizeRead st (chunkSize l 0 0 0) k
lineRead ChunkEnd st l k =
  if Bytes.length l == 0 then StepOn { st | at = SizeLine } k
  else Stepped (ChunksRefused 400)
lineRead InTrailer st l k =
  if Bytes.length l == 0 then TrailerRead st k
  else if st.trailer + Bytes.length l > headMost
  then Stepped (ChunksRefused 400)
  else StepOn { st | trailer = st.trailer + Bytes.length l } k
lineRead (InChunk n) st l k = Stepped (ChunksRefused 400)

-- (how long a line may be where the body is read to: the trailer's, as
-- a head may be; another, `chunkLineMost`, its CRLF too)
lineMostAt : ChunkAt -> Int
lineMostAt InTrailer = headMost
lineMostAt at = chunkLineMost

-- (a line read of `b` from `k` on, after what was read of it before: up
-- to its CRLF, and the line taken; else kept, to be read on with the
-- next piece.  Longer than it may be, or its line feed not after a
-- carriage return, `400`)
lineIn : Chunks -> Bytes -> Int -> ChunkStep
lineIn st b k =
  let j = lineFeedIn b k
  in let l =
    Bytes.append
      st.line
      (Bytes.slice b k (if j < 0 then Bytes.length b else j + 1))
  in if Bytes.length l > lineMostAt st.at then Stepped (ChunksRefused 400)
  else if j < 0 then StepOn { st | line = l } (Bytes.length b)
  else if Bytes.length l < 2 || not (byteIs l (Bytes.length l - 2) 13)
  then Stepped (ChunksRefused 400)
  else lineRead
      st.at
      { st | line = Bytes.empty }
      (Bytes.slice l 0 (Bytes.length l - 2))
      (j + 1)

-- (a chunk's data, `n` bytes of it to come, read of `b` from `k` on: as
-- much as is there of it, taken)
dataIn : Chunks -> Int -> Bytes -> Int -> ChunkStep
dataIn st n b k =
  let m : Int = if n < Bytes.length b - k then n else Bytes.length b - k
  in StepOn
    { st
    | at = if m == n then ChunkEnd else InChunk (n - m)
    , taken = Bytes.slice b k (k + m) :: st.taken
    }
    (k + m)

stepAt : ChunkAt -> Chunks -> Bytes -> Int -> ChunkStep
stepAt (InChunk n) st b k = dataIn st n b k
stepAt at st b k = lineIn st b k

-- (the data taken of a piece, put with the data before it: one part, so
-- that a body of many small chunks is no list of as many)
joined : List Bytes -> List Bytes -> List Bytes
joined [] parts = parts
joined [p] parts = p :: parts
joined taken parts = Bytes.concat (List.reverse taken) :: parts

flushed : Chunks -> Chunks
flushed st = { st | parts = joined st.taken st.parts, taken = Nil }

-- (a piece `b` read on, a step of it taken: from where it got to, to
-- the piece's end; the body, all read, and the piece's rest; or done)
fedOn : Bytes -> ChunkStep -> Dechunked
fedOn b (StepOn st k) =
  if k >= Bytes.length b then ChunksToCome (flushed st)
  else fedOn b (stepAt st.at st b k)
fedOn b (TrailerRead done at) =
  BodyRead
    (Bytes.concat (List.reverse (flushed done).parts))
    (Bytes.slice b at (Bytes.length b))
fedOn b (Stepped d) = d

-- (pieces fed, one after another, while more is to come)
fedAll : Dechunked -> List Bytes -> Dechunked
fedAll (ChunksToCome st) (b :: bs) = fedAll (fedOn b (StepOn st 0)) bs
fedAll d bs = d

dechunkedSaid : Dechunked -> String
dechunkedSaid (BodyRead body rest) = show body ^ ", then " ^ show rest
dechunkedSaid (ChunksToCome st) = "to come, " ^ debug st.size ^ " bytes so far"
dechunkedSaid (ChunksRefused status) = "refused, " ^ debug status

-- (a body's pieces read, what they come to said: for the examples)
chunksSaid : List Bytes -> String
chunksSaid pieces = dechunkedSaid (fedAll (ChunksToCome chunks) pieces)

-- | A piece more of a body sent in chunks read, `Transfer-Encoding:
-- | chunked` as RFC 9112 says it: each chunk its size in hexadecimal,
-- | its extensions, if any, not minded, a line's end, its data and a
-- | line's end; the last of size 0, then the trailer, its fields let go
-- | of, and a blank line.  Its data more than a body's most, 64 MiB,
-- | `413`; a line not so, a chunk's size line longer than 4 KiB or a
-- | trailer longer than a head may be, `400`.
-- | >>> chunksSaid [b["3\r\nabc\r\n4\r\ndefg\r\n0\r\n\r\n"]]
-- | "abcdefg, then "
-- | >>> chunksSaid [b["3\r"], b["\nab"], b["c\r\n1;name=\"v\" ; x\r\n"], b["d\r\n0\r\n\r"], b["\n"]]
-- | "abcd, then "
-- | >>> chunksSaid [b["3\r\nabc\r\n0\r\nExpires: never\r\nX-Sum: 1\r\n\r\nGET / HTTP/1.1\r\n"]]
-- | "abc, then GET / HTTP/1.1\r\n"
-- | >>> chunksSaid [b["A\r\n0123456789\r\n"], b["0\r\n"]]
-- | "to come, 10 bytes so far"
-- | >>> chunksSaid [b["4000000\r\n"]]
-- | "to come, 67108864 bytes so far"
-- | >>> chunksSaid [b["4000001\r\n"]]
-- | "refused, 413"
-- | >>> chunksSaid [b["fffffffffffffffffffff\r\n"]]
-- | "refused, 413"
-- | >>> List.map (\(t : String) -> chunksSaid [Bytes.fromString t]) ["x\r\n", "\r\n", "3 \r\n", "3\nabc", "3\r\nabcd\r\n", "-3\r\n"]
-- | ["refused, 400", "refused, 400", "refused, 400", "refused, 400", "refused, 400", "refused, 400"]
-- | >>> chunksSaid [Bytes.fromString ("1;" ^ joinWith "" (List.replicate 4096 "x"))]
-- | "refused, 400"
feedChunks : Chunks -> Bytes -> Dechunked
feedChunks st b = fedOn b (StepOn st 0)

-- (more bytes after `buf`: `again` of them all; where the connection
-- ended, or failed, `ended`)
moreBytes : {e : HFunctor}
          -> {a : Type}
          -> (Bytes -> Co e a)
          -> a
          -> Bytes
          -> Either Net.NetError Bytes
          -> Co e a
moreBytes again ended buf (Left err) = pure ended
moreBytes again ended buf (Right b) =
  if Bytes.length b == 0 then pure ended else again (Bytes.append buf b)

-- (a head read: the bytes read, and where its blank line starts)
data HeadRead = HeadAt Bytes Int | HeadTooLong | HeadEnded

-- (the monotonic clock, in milliseconds)
millisecondsNow : {e : HFunctor} -> {{clock : Time.time <: e}} -> Co e Int
millisecondsNow =
  bind Time.monotonic (\d -> pure (Duration.totalNanoseconds d / 1000000))

-- (when a head begun now is to be read by, on the monotonic clock, given
-- `within` milliseconds for it: none where that is 0)
headBy : {e : HFunctor}
       -> {{clock : Time.time <: e}}
       -> Int
       -> Co e (Maybe Int)
headBy 0 = pure Nothing
headBy within = bind millisecondsNow (\now -> pure (Just (now + within)))

-- (the shorter of two time limits, 0 none)
shorter : Int -> Int -> Int
shorter 0 left = left
shorter idle left = if idle < left then idle else left

-- (more of a head read, `size` bytes at most, within `idle`
-- milliseconds, and by `by` on the monotonic clock where there is a
-- `by`: where that has passed, none, as where the connection ends)
headRead : {e : HFunctor}
         -> {s : Type}
         -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
         -> {{clock : Time.time <: e}}
         -> Int
         -> Maybe Int
         -> With s Net.TcpStream
         -> Int
         -> Co e (Either Net.NetError Bytes)
headRead idle Nothing c size = Net.read (timeout := idle) c size
headRead idle (Just by) c size =
  bind
    millisecondsNow
    (\now ->
       if now >= by then pure (Right Bytes.empty)
       else Net.read (timeout := shorter idle (by - now)) c size)

-- (bytes read until `buf` has a head, looked for from `from` on, each
-- read within `idle` milliseconds, and all by `by`; where one is not,
-- the connection's end)
readHead : {e : HFunctor}
         -> {s : Type}
         -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
         -> {{clock : Time.time <: e}}
         -> Int
         -> Maybe Int
         -> With s Net.TcpStream
         -> Bytes
         -> Int
         -> Co e HeadRead
readHead idle by c buf from =
  let i = headEnd buf from
  in if i >= 0 then pure (HeadAt buf i)
  else if Bytes.length buf > headMost then pure HeadTooLong
  else let next : Int = if Bytes.length buf > 3 then Bytes.length buf - 3 else 0
       in bind
         (headRead
            idle
            by
            c
            (if Bytes.length buf == 0 then readSize else headPiece))
         (moreBytes (\b -> readHead idle by c b next) HeadEnded buf)

-- (a read's bytes, after the parts before, `got` bytes in all: `again`
-- of them; where the connection ended, or failed, none)
moreBody : {e : HFunctor}
         -> (Int -> List Bytes -> Co e (Maybe Bytes))
         -> Int
         -> List Bytes
         -> Either Net.NetError Bytes
         -> Co e (Maybe Bytes)
moreBody again got parts (Left err) = pure Nothing
moreBody again got parts (Right b) =
  if Bytes.length b == 0 then pure Nothing
  else again (got + Bytes.length b) (b :: parts)

-- (bytes read until there are `n` at least, `got` of them in `parts`,
-- the last first: all of them; none where the connection ends first)
readBody : {e : HFunctor}
         -> {s : Type}
         -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
         -> Int
         -> With s Net.TcpStream
         -> Int
         -> Int
         -> List Bytes
         -> Co e (Maybe Bytes)
readBody idle c n got parts =
  if got >= n then pure (Just (Bytes.concat (List.reverse parts)))
  else bind
      (Net.read (timeout := idle) c (n - got))
      (moreBody (readBody idle c n) got parts)

-- (what reading a request came to: the request, and what was read after
-- it; a status it is answered with, the connection then closed; or the
-- connection's end)
data Got = Asked Request Bytes | Refused Int | Ended

bodied : Request -> Int -> Maybe Bytes -> Got
bodied r n Nothing = Ended
bodied r n (Just b) =
  Asked { r | body = Bytes.slice b 0 n } (Bytes.slice b n (Bytes.length b))

-- | What a request not all read yet wants: more of its head, so many
-- | bytes in all at least (`MoreHead`); its head read, more of its body,
-- | so many bytes in all, the head's too (`MoreBody`); or its head read,
-- | more of its body sent in chunks, read so far (`MoreChunks`), each
-- | piece read after given to `feedChunks`.
data Wanted = MoreHead Int | MoreBody Request Int | MoreChunks Request Chunks

-- (what a request whose head is read comes to: `buf` read of it, its
-- body from `at` on)
bodyIn : Request -> Bytes -> Int -> BodyIs -> Either Wanted Got
bodyIn r buf at (Refuse status) = Right (Refused status)
bodyIn r buf at (Length n) =
  if Bytes.length buf < at + n then Left (MoreBody r (at + n))
  else Right (bodied r n (Just (Bytes.slice buf at (Bytes.length buf))))
bodyIn r buf at Chunked =
  dechunkedIn r (feedChunks chunks (Bytes.slice buf at (Bytes.length buf)))
  where
  dechunkedIn : Request -> Dechunked -> Either Wanted Got
  dechunkedIn r (BodyRead body rest) = Right (Asked { r | body = body } rest)
  dechunkedIn r (ChunksToCome st) = Left (MoreChunks r st)
  dechunkedIn r (ChunksRefused status) = Right (Refused status)

-- (what reading a request came to, said: for the examples)
wantedSaid : Either Wanted Got -> String
wantedSaid (Left (MoreHead n)) = "head, " ^ debug n
wantedSaid (Left (MoreBody r n)) = "body, " ^ debug n
wantedSaid (Left (MoreChunks r st)) = "chunks, " ^ debug st.size
wantedSaid (Right (Asked r rest)) = show r.body ^ ", then " ^ show rest
wantedSaid (Right (Refused status)) = "refused, " ^ debug status
wantedSaid (Right Ended) = "ended"

-- | What the bytes read so far of a connection's next request come to,
-- | read all at once, not waiting for more (a server that reads a piece
-- | at a time asks after each): the request, and what was read after
-- | it (`Asked`), or the status it is answered with (`Refused`); else,
-- | not all read yet, `Left`, what it wants (`Wanted`).  The head's end,
-- | its blank line, is looked for from `from` on, by name (0, the start,
-- | unless another is given): a reader that has looked through what
-- | came before, or knows where it is, says so.
-- | >>> wantedSaid (requestIn { host = "::1", port = 1 } b["GET / HTTP/1.1\r\nContent-Length: 3\r\n\r\nab"])
-- | "body, 40"
-- | >>> wantedSaid (requestIn { host = "::1", port = 1 } b["GET / HTTP/1.1\r\nContent-Length: 3\r\n\r\nabcGET"])
-- | "abc, then GET"
-- | >>> wantedSaid (requestIn (from := 14) { host = "::1", port = 1 } b["GET / HTTP/1.1\r\n\r\n"])
-- | ", then "
-- | >>> wantedSaid (requestIn { host = "::1", port = 1 } b["POST / HTTP/1.1\r\nTransfer-Encoding: chunked\r\n\r\n3\r\nab"])
-- | "chunks, 3"
-- | >>> wantedSaid (requestIn { host = "::1", port = 1 } b["POST / HTTP/1.1\r\nTransfer-Encoding: chunked\r\n\r\n3\r\nabc\r\n0\r\n\r\nGET"])
-- | "abc, then GET"
-- | >>> List.map (\(h : String) -> wantedSaid (requestIn { host = "::1", port = 1 } (Bytes.fromString ("POST / HTTP/1.1\r\n" ^ h ^ "\r\n\r\n")))) ["Transfer-Encoding: gzip", "Transfer-Encoding: gzip, chunked", "Transfer-Encoding: chunked\r\nContent-Length: 0", "Transfer-Encoding: chunked, chunked", "Transfer-Encoding: Chunked\r\nTransfer-Encoding: gzip"]
-- | ["refused, 501", "refused, 501", "refused, 400", "refused, 400", "refused, 501"]
requestIn : {from : Int := 0} -> Net.Address -> Bytes -> Either Wanted Got
requestIn peer buf =
  let i = headEnd buf from
  in if i < 0
  then (if Bytes.length buf > headMost then Right (Refused 431)
        else Left (MoreHead (Bytes.length buf + 1)))
  else case parseHead peer (show (Bytes.slice buf 0 i)) of
    Nothing -> Right (Refused 400)
    Just r -> bodyIn r buf (i + 4) (bodyOf r)

-- (whether more of a body sent in chunks is to come)
toCome : Dechunked -> Bool
toCome (ChunksToCome st) = True
toCome d = False

-- (a read's bytes, `again` of them; where the connection ended, or
-- failed, its end)
moreChunks : {e : HFunctor}
           -> (Bytes -> Co e Got)
           -> Either Net.NetError Bytes
           -> Co e Got
moreChunks again (Left err) = pure Ended
moreChunks again (Right b) = if Bytes.length b == 0 then pure Ended else again b

-- (a body sent in chunks read, a piece at a time, each read within
-- `idle` milliseconds, until it is all read: the request, its body the
-- chunks' data, and what was read after it; or the status it is
-- answered with; or, the connection ended first, its end)
readChunks : {e : HFunctor}
           -> {s : Type}
           -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
           -> Int
           -> With s Net.TcpStream
           -> Request
           -> Dechunked
           -> Co e Got
readChunks idle c r (BodyRead body rest) = pure (Asked { r | body = body } rest)
readChunks idle c r (ChunksRefused status) = pure (Refused status)
readChunks idle c r (ChunksToCome st) =
  bind
    (Net.read (timeout := idle) c readSize)
    (moreChunks (\b -> readChunks idle c r (feedChunks st b)))

-- (the request whose head ends at `i` of `buf`, its body read)
withBody : {e : HFunctor}
         -> {s : Type}
         -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
         -> Int
         -> With s Net.TcpStream
         -> Bytes
         -> Int
         -> Request
         -> BodyIs
         -> Co e Got
withBody idle c buf i r (Refuse status) = pure (Refused status)
withBody idle c buf i r (Length n) = do
  let rest = Bytes.slice buf (i + 4) (Bytes.length buf)
  w <-
    (if n > Bytes.length rest && expects r
     then Net.write (timeout := idle) c b["HTTP/1.1 100 Continue\r\n\r\n"]
     else pure (Right MkUnit))
  got <- readBody idle c n (Bytes.length rest) [rest]
  pure (bodied r n got)
withBody idle c buf i r Chunked = do
  let fed = feedChunks chunks (Bytes.slice buf (i + 4) (Bytes.length buf))
  w <-
    (if toCome fed && expects r
     then Net.write (timeout := idle) c b["HTTP/1.1 100 Continue\r\n\r\n"]
     else pure (Right MkUnit))
  readChunks idle c r fed

parsed : {e : HFunctor}
       -> {s : Type}
       -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
       -> Int
       -> With s Net.TcpStream
       -> Bytes
       -> Int
       -> Maybe Request
       -> Co e Got
parsed idle c buf i Nothing = pure (Refused 400)
parsed idle c buf i (Just r) = withBody idle c buf i r (bodyOf r)

headed : {e : HFunctor}
       -> {s : Type}
       -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
       -> Int
       -> With s Net.TcpStream
       -> Net.Address
       -> HeadRead
       -> Co e Got
headed idle c peer (HeadAt buf i) =
  parsed idle c buf i (parseHead peer (show (Bytes.slice buf 0 i)))
headed idle c peer HeadTooLong = pure (Refused 431)
headed idle c peer HeadEnded = pure Ended

-- (the next request of the connection, `buf` read of it already, each
-- read within `idle` milliseconds, and its head within `within` of now)
readRequest : {e : HFunctor}
            -> {s : Type}
            -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
            -> {{clock : Time.time <: e}}
            -> Int
            -> Int
            -> With s Net.TcpStream
            -> Net.Address
            -> Bytes
            -> Co e Got
readRequest idle within c peer buf = do
  by <- headBy within
  head <- readHead idle by c buf 0
  headed idle c peer head

-- Writing a response
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- | A status's reason, as a status line says it (`OK`, `Not Found`); a
-- | status not known, none.
reason : Int -> String
reason 100 = "Continue"
reason 101 = "Switching Protocols"
reason 200 = "OK"
reason 201 = "Created"
reason 202 = "Accepted"
reason 204 = "No Content"
reason 206 = "Partial Content"
reason 301 = "Moved Permanently"
reason 302 = "Found"
reason 303 = "See Other"
reason 304 = "Not Modified"
reason 307 = "Temporary Redirect"
reason 308 = "Permanent Redirect"
reason 400 = "Bad Request"
reason 401 = "Unauthorized"
reason 403 = "Forbidden"
reason 404 = "Not Found"
reason 405 = "Method Not Allowed"
reason 408 = "Request Timeout"
reason 409 = "Conflict"
reason 410 = "Gone"
reason 411 = "Length Required"
reason 413 = "Content Too Large"
reason 414 = "URI Too Long"
reason 415 = "Unsupported Media Type"
reason 422 = "Unprocessable Content"
reason 429 = "Too Many Requests"
reason 431 = "Request Header Fields Too Large"
reason 500 = "Internal Server Error"
reason 501 = "Not Implemented"
reason 502 = "Bad Gateway"
reason 503 = "Service Unavailable"
reason 504 = "Gateway Timeout"
reason 505 = "HTTP Version Not Supported"
reason _ = ""

-- (a status whose response has no body: 1xx, 204, 304)
bodiless : Int -> Bool
bodiless s = s < 200 || s == 204 || s == 304

-- (a header the server writes itself: the length, and the connection)
ownHeader : Pair String String -> Bool
ownHeader (MkPair n v) =
  HTTP.sameName n "Content-Length"
  || HTTP.sameName n "Transfer-Encoding"
  || HTTP.sameName n "Connection"

headerText : String -> Pair String String -> String
headerText acc (MkPair n v) = acc ^ n ^ ": " ^ v ^ "\r\n"

-- (a status line)
statusLine : Int -> String
statusLine status = "HTTP/1.1 " ^ debug status ^ " " ^ reason status ^ "\r\n"

-- (a head: its status line, its headers but the server's own, the
-- server's own lines, `own`, and the blank line after them)
headWith : Int -> List (Pair String String) -> String -> String
headWith status headers own =
  statusLine status
  ^ List.foldl headerText "" (List.keepIf (\h -> not (ownHeader h)) headers)
  ^ own
  ^ "\r\n"

-- (`Connection: connection`, where that is not empty)
connectionLine : String -> String
connectionLine "" = ""
connectionLine connection = "Connection: " ^ connection ^ "\r\n"

-- | A response as it is written: its status line, its headers but its
-- | own length and connection, its length (`Content-Length`, where its
-- | status has a body), `Connection: connection` where that is not
-- | empty, and its body where `withBody` (not for a `HEAD`).
-- | >>> debug (responseBytes "close" True (plain 200 "hi"))
-- | "b[\"HTTP/1.1 200 OK\", 13, 10, \"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\", 13, 10, \"Content-Length: 2\", 13, 10, \"Connection: close\", 13, 10, 13, 10, \"hi\"]"
-- | >>> debug (responseBytes "" False { status = 204, headers = [MkPair "Content-Length" "9"], body = b["x"] })
-- | "b[\"HTTP/1.1 204 No Content\", 13, 10, 13, 10]"
responseBytes : String -> Bool -> HTTP.Response -> Bytes
responseBytes connection withBody res =
  let none = bodiless res.status
  in let head =
    headWith
      res.status
      res.headers
      ((if none then ""
        else "Content-Length: " ^ debug (Bytes.length res.body) ^ "\r\n")
       ^ connectionLine connection)
  in if withBody && not none then Bytes.append (Bytes.fromString head) res.body
  else Bytes.fromString head

-- (a digit of hexadecimal, 0 to 15)
hexDigit : Int -> String
hexDigit d = strSlice "0123456789abcdef" d (d + 1)

-- (`n`, not negative, in hexadecimal)
hexOf : Int -> String
hexOf n = if n < 16 then hexDigit n else hexOf (n / 16) ^ hexDigit (n % 16)

-- | A piece of a streamed body as it is written to an HTTP/1.1 request,
-- | a chunk of `Transfer-Encoding: chunked`: its length in hexadecimal,
-- | then the piece, each ended by a line's end.  (A piece of no bytes is
-- | the last chunk, which ends the body: the server writes none of the
-- | body's so.)
-- | >>> debug (chunk b["hello, world, and the rest"])
-- | "b[\"1a\", 13, 10, \"hello, world, and the rest\", 13, 10]"
chunk : Bytes -> Bytes
chunk b =
  Bytes.concat
    [Bytes.fromString (hexOf (Bytes.length b) ^ "\r\n"), b, b["\r\n"]]

-- | What a reply that is not whole begins with, before its body or the
-- | connection taken over: its status, and its headers.
type Head = { status : Int, headers : List (Pair String String) }

-- | A streamed reply's head as it is written: its status line, its
-- | headers but its own length and connection, `Transfer-Encoding:
-- | chunked` where `chunked`, and `Connection: connection` where that is
-- | not empty.
-- | >>> debug (streamedHead "" True { status = 200, headers = [MkPair "Content-Type" "text/event-stream", MkPair "Content-Length" "3"] })
-- | "b[\"HTTP/1.1 200 OK\", 13, 10, \"Content-Type: text/event-stream\", 13, 10, \"Transfer-Encoding: chunked\", 13, 10, 13, 10]"
-- | >>> debug (streamedHead "close" False { status = 200, headers = Nil })
-- | "b[\"HTTP/1.1 200 OK\", 13, 10, \"Connection: close\", 13, 10, 13, 10]"
streamedHead : String -> Bool -> Head -> Bytes
streamedHead connection chunked head =
  Bytes.fromString
    (headWith
       head.status
       head.headers
       ((if chunked then "Transfer-Encoding: chunked\r\n" else "")
        ^ connectionLine connection))

-- | The head written before a connection is taken over: its status line
-- | and its headers, all as they are given, `Connection` too -- no
-- | length, nothing of the server's.
-- | >>> debug (takeoverHead { status = 101, headers = [MkPair "Connection" "Upgrade", MkPair "Upgrade" "websocket"] })
-- | "b[\"HTTP/1.1 101 Switching Protocols\", 13, 10, \"Connection: Upgrade\", 13, 10, \"Upgrade: websocket\", 13, 10, 13, 10]"
takeoverHead : Head -> Bytes
takeoverHead head =
  Bytes.fromString
    (statusLine head.status ^ List.foldl headerText "" head.headers ^ "\r\n")

-- (whether a `Connection` header of these has the token, its case not
-- minded)
connectionSays : String -> List (Pair String String) -> Bool
connectionSays token [] = False
connectionSays token (MkPair n v :: rest) =
  (HTTP.sameName n "Connection"
   && List.any (\t -> HTTP.sameName (trim t) token) (split "," v))
  || connectionSays token rest

-- | Whether a request's connection is kept after its response, as the
-- | request asks: HTTP/1.1's unless it says `Connection: close`,
-- | HTTP/1.0's where it says `Connection: keep-alive`.
keptAlive : Request -> Bool
keptAlive r =
  if strEq r.version "HTTP/1.1" then not (connectionSays "close" r.headers)
  else connectionSays "keep-alive" r.headers

-- (what a response says of its connection: closed, or kept where
-- HTTP/1.0 has to be told so)
connectionWord : Request -> Bool -> String
connectionWord r True = "close"
connectionWord r False = if strEq r.version "HTTP/1.0" then "keep-alive" else ""

-- Serving
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (what a request answered came to: the connection's next request, what
-- was read of it already; or the connection done, and whether the
-- server stops)
data After = Next Bytes | Done Bool

afterWrite : Bytes -> Bool -> Bool -> Either Net.NetError Unit -> After
afterWrite rest close stop (Left err) = Done stop
afterWrite rest close stop (Right _) = if close then Done stop else Next rest

-- (what a read came to, `got` bytes let go of before it: `again`; at
-- the end of what the client sends, or where reading failed, done)
drainedOn : {e : HFunctor}
          -> (Int -> Co e Unit)
          -> Int
          -> Either Net.NetError Bytes
          -> Co e Unit
drainedOn again got (Left err) = pure MkUnit
drainedOn again got (Right b) =
  if Bytes.length b == 0 then pure MkUnit else again (got + Bytes.length b)

-- (what the client sends read and let go of, `got` bytes of it already,
-- until it ends or there has been `drainMost` of it)
drain : {e : HFunctor}
      -> {s : Type}
      -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
      -> Int
      -> With s Net.TcpStream
      -> Int
      -> Co e Unit
drain idle c got =
  if got >= drainMost then pure MkUnit
  else bind
      (Net.read (timeout := idle) c readSize)
      (drainedOn (drain idle c) got)

-- (a refusal written: this side shut down, so that the client reads the
-- response to its end, and what it still sends drained, so that the
-- connection closed with bytes unread -- a reset, which may come before
-- the client has read the response -- is not what it is sent)
lingered : {e : HFunctor}
         -> {s : Type}
         -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
         -> Int
         -> With s Net.TcpStream
         -> Either Net.NetError Unit
         -> Co e Unit
lingered idle c (Left err) = pure MkUnit
lingered idle c (Right _) = bind (Net.shutdown c) (\s -> drain idle c 0)

-- (whether a request's connection is closed after its reply, whose
-- headers are these: as the request asks, as the reply says, or as
-- `last` says the server stops)
closes : (Request -> Bool) -> Request -> List (Pair String String) -> Bool
closes last r headers =
  last r || not (keptAlive r) || connectionSays "close" headers

-- (a response, whole, written)
wholeOut : {e : HFunctor}
         -> {s : Type}
         -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
         -> Int
         -> With s Net.TcpStream
         -> (Request -> Bool)
         -> Request
         -> Bytes
         -> HTTP.Response
         -> Co e After
wholeOut idle c last r rest res = do
  let close = closes last r res.headers
  w <-
    Net.write
      (timeout := idle)
      c
      (responseBytes (connectionWord r close) (not (strEq r.method "HEAD")) res)
  pure (afterWrite rest close (last r) w)

-- | What a handler answers a request with, its connection `taken over`:
-- | the request, the connection, and what was read of it after the
-- | request -- the start of what the other side sent next, which the
-- | server read with the request and did not use.
type Taken s =
  { request : Request
  , connection : With s Net.TcpStream
  , rest : Bytes
  }

-- | What a handler answers a request with: a response, whole
-- | (`Whole`); a head (a status and headers) and a body that yields its
-- | pieces (`Streamed`), each written as it is yielded; or a head, after
-- | which the connection is the function's (`TakenOver`),
-- | given the request, the connection and what was read after the
-- | request.  A streamed reply's headers and a whole one's give no
-- | length, `Transfer-Encoding` or `Connection` of their own -- the
-- | server writes those -- but `Connection: close`, which closes the
-- | connection after the reply; a connection taken over is written its
-- | headers as they are.
data Reply (e : HFunctor)
  = Whole HTTP.Response
  | Streamed Head (Co (Stream.yielding Bytes <+> e) Unit)
  | TakenOver Head ({s : Type} -> Taken s -> Co e Unit)

-- (a piece of a streamed body written, a chunk where `chunked`: none of
-- no bytes, which would end the chunks; where it is not written, why
-- thrown)
pieceOut : {e : HFunctor}
         -> {s : Type}
         -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
         -> {{ex : exception Net.NetError <: e}}
         -> Int
         -> With s Net.TcpStream
         -> Bool
         -> Bytes
         -> Co e Unit
pieceOut idle c chunked b =
  if Bytes.length b == 0 then pure MkUnit
  else bind
      (Net.write (timeout := idle) c (if chunked then chunk b else b))
      (either throw pure)

-- (a streamed body's `yield`: its piece written)
pieceWritten : {e : HFunctor}
             -> {s : Type}
             -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
             -> {{ex : exception Net.NetError <: e}}
             -> Int
             -> With s Net.TcpStream
             -> Bool
             -> {a : Type}
             -> Stream.YieldF Bytes (Co e) a
             -> Co e a
pieceWritten idle c chunked (Yield b x) =
  bind (pieceOut idle c chunked b) (\u -> pure x)

-- (whether the last chunk is written, where there is one)
endWritten : Either Net.NetError Unit -> Bool
endWritten (Left err) = False
endWritten (Right u) = True

-- (a streamed body run, each piece written as it is yielded, and the
-- last chunk after them where `chunked`: whether all of it was written;
-- not where a write failed, or the body threw a `NetError` of its own)
bodyOut : {e : HFunctor}
        -> {s : Type}
        -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
        -> {{ex : exception Net.NetError <: e}}
        -> Int
        -> With s Net.TcpStream
        -> Bool
        -> Co (Stream.yielding Bytes <+> e) Unit
        -> Co e Bool
bodyOut idle c chunked body = do
  try
    handle
        (through (Stream.yielding Bytes) e (pieceWritten idle c chunked))
        body
    ended <-
      (if chunked then Net.write (timeout := idle) c b["0\r\n\r\n"]
       else pure (Right MkUnit))
    pure (endWritten ended)
  catch (err : Net.NetError) ->
    pure False

-- (what a streamed reply came to, its body written, `written` whether
-- all of it was)
afterBody : Bytes -> Bool -> Bool -> Bool -> After
afterBody rest close stop written =
  if written && not close then Next rest else Done stop

-- (a streamed reply's head written, `w`: its body after it, where it is
-- `sent`)
headOut : {e : HFunctor}
        -> {s : Type}
        -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
        -> {{ex : exception Net.NetError <: e}}
        -> Int
        -> With s Net.TcpStream
        -> Bool
        -> Bool
        -> Co (Stream.yielding Bytes <+> e) Unit
        -> Bytes
        -> Bool
        -> Bool
        -> Either Net.NetError Unit
        -> Co e After
headOut idle c chunked sent body rest close stop (Left err) = pure (Done stop)
headOut idle c chunked False body rest close stop (Right u) =
  pure (afterBody rest close stop True)
headOut idle c chunked True body rest close stop (Right u) =
  bind (bodyOut idle c chunked body) (\w -> pure (afterBody rest close stop w))

-- (a streamed reply written: in chunks to HTTP/1.1, the connection
-- closed after it to HTTP/1.0, which has no other end of it; to a
-- `HEAD`, or of a status with no body, its head alone)
streamedOut : {e : HFunctor}
            -> {s : Type}
            -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
            -> {{ex : exception Net.NetError <: e}}
            -> Int
            -> With s Net.TcpStream
            -> (Request -> Bool)
            -> Request
            -> Bytes
            -> Head
            -> Co (Stream.yielding Bytes <+> e) Unit
            -> Co e After
streamedOut idle c last r rest head body = do
  let chunked = strEq r.version "HTTP/1.1"
  let close = not chunked || closes last r head.headers
  let none = bodiless head.status
  w <-
    Net.write
      (timeout := idle)
      c
      (streamedHead (connectionWord r close) (chunked && not none) head)
  headOut
      idle
      c
      chunked
      (not none && not (strEq r.method "HEAD"))
      body
      rest
      close
      (last r)
      w

-- (the head written, `w`: the connection handed over, the server done
-- with it after)
handedOver : {e : HFunctor}
           -> Co e Unit
           -> Bool
           -> Either Net.NetError Unit
           -> Co e After
handedOver taken stop (Left err) = pure (Done stop)
handedOver taken stop (Right u) = bind taken (\v -> pure (Done stop))

-- (what a handler replied, written)
replied : {e : HFunctor}
        -> {s : Type}
        -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
        -> {{ex : exception Net.NetError <: e}}
        -> Int
        -> With s Net.TcpStream
        -> (Request -> Bool)
        -> Request
        -> Bytes
        -> Reply e
        -> Co e After
replied idle c last r rest (Whole res) = wholeOut idle c last r rest res
replied idle c last r rest (Streamed head body) =
  streamedOut idle c last r rest head body
replied idle c last r rest (TakenOver head f) =
  bind
    (Net.write (timeout := idle) c (takeoverHead head))
    (handedOver (f { request = r, connection = c, rest = rest }) (last r))

-- (what was read, answered: a request by `answer`, given what was read
-- after it)
answered : {e : HFunctor}
         -> {s : Type}
         -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
         -> Int
         -> With s Net.TcpStream
         -> (Request -> Bytes -> Co e After)
         -> Got
         -> Co e After
answered idle c answer (Asked r rest) = answer r rest
answered idle c answer (Refused status) = do
  w <-
    Net.write
      (timeout := idle)
      c
      (responseBytes "close" True (plain status (reason status ^ "\n")))
  lingered idle c w
  pure (Done False)
answered idle c answer Ended = pure (Done False)

-- (the connection's next request, `again`; or it is done: whether the
-- server stops)
goOn : {e : HFunctor} -> (Bytes -> Co e Bool) -> After -> Co e Bool
goOn again (Next rest) = again rest
goOn again (Done stop) = pure stop

closedWith : {e : HFunctor}
           -> {s : Type}
           -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
           -> {{clock : Time.time <: e}}
           -> Int
           -> Int
           -> (Request -> Bytes -> Co e After)
           -> With s Net.TcpStream
           -> Either Net.NetError Net.Address
           -> Co e Bool
closedWith idle within answer c (Left err) = pure False
closedWith idle within answer c (Right peer) = serveFrom Bytes.empty
  where
  -- (the connection's requests answered, `buf` read of them already)
  serveFrom : Bytes -> Co e Bool
  serveFrom buf = do
    got <- readRequest idle within c peer buf
    after <- answered idle c answer got
    goOn serveFrom after

-- | A connection's requests answered by `handle`, one after another,
-- | each with a `Reply` -- a response whole, one streamed, or the
-- | connection taken over, the server done with it once the function it
-- | is given is -- until it ends, a request asks for it to be closed, or
-- | `last` says the request is the last the server answers: whether
-- | `last` said so.  The connection is closed by the `with` holding it,
-- | `Net.accept`'s or `Net.withConnection`'s, when its body ends.  Where
-- | the client sends nothing for `idle` milliseconds, it ends there (0:
-- | no limit); where a request's head is not all read within
-- | `headerWithin` milliseconds of the connection's start, or of the
-- | response before it, too (0: no limit).
serveConnection : {e : HFunctor}
                -> {s : Type}
                -> {idle : Int := 30000}
                -> {headerWithin : Int := 30000}
                -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
                -> {{clock : Time.time <: e}}
                -> {{ex : exception Net.NetError <: e}}
                -> (Request -> Bool)
                -> (Request -> Co e (Reply e))
                -> With s Net.TcpStream
                -> Co e Bool
serveConnection last handle c =
  bind
    (Net.peer c)
    (closedWith
       idle
       headerWithin
       (\r rest -> bind (handle r) (replied idle c last r rest))
       c)

-- (the next connection, `again`; or the server done, `last` said so)
nextOr : {e : HFunctor} -> (Unit -> Co e Unit) -> Bool -> Co e Unit
nextOr again True = pure MkUnit
nextOr again False = again MkUnit

-- | The listener's connections accepted, one at a time, and each one's
-- | requests answered by `handle` (`serveConnection`), until `last` says
-- | a request is the last: answered, its connection closed, and the
-- | listener left as it is.  Where a connection fails to be accepted --
-- | the system out of descriptors (`EMFILE`), say -- the server stops
-- | there, why thrown (`Net.accept`'s `NetError`), the listener left as
-- | it is: whether to wait and serve again is its caller's to say.
serveUntil : {e : HFunctor}
           -> {s : Type}
           -> {idle : Int := 30000}
           -> {headerWithin : Int := 30000}
           -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
           -> {{clock : Time.time <: e}}
           -> {{ex : exception Net.NetError <: e}}
           -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: e}}
           -> (Request -> Bool)
           -> With s Net.TcpListener
           -> (Request -> Co e (Reply e))
           -> Co e Unit
serveUntil last l handle =
  bind
    (Net.accept
       l
       (serveConnection
          (idle := idle)
          (headerWithin := headerWithin)
          last
          handle))
    (nextOr
       (\u ->
          serveUntil
            (idle := idle)
            (headerWithin := headerWithin)
            last
            l
            handle))

-- | The listener's connections served, until one fails to be accepted:
-- | why thrown, the listener left as it is (`serveUntil`).
serve : {e : HFunctor}
      -> {s : Type}
      -> {idle : Int := 30000}
      -> {headerWithin : Int := 30000}
      -> {{nt : Net.net <: e}}
      -> {{clock : Time.time <: e}}
      -> {{ex : exception Net.NetError <: e}}
      -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: e}}
      -> With s Net.TcpListener
      -> (Request -> Co e (Reply e))
      -> Co e Unit
serve l handle =
  bind
    (Net.accept
       l
       (serveConnection
          (idle := idle)
          (headerWithin := headerWithin)
          (\r -> False)
          handle))
    (\stop -> serve (idle := idle) (headerWithin := headerWithin) l handle)
